Important Viva Questions and Answers
Q1. What is data wrangling?

Data wrangling is the process of cleaning, transforming and organizing raw data into a useful format for analysis.

Q2. What is the difference between data cleaning and data wrangling?

Data cleaning focuses on correcting missing, duplicate and incorrect data. Data wrangling includes cleaning as well as transforming and organizing data.

Q3. What is filtering?

Filtering is the process of selecting records based on specific conditions.

Q4. What is the use of groupby()?

It groups data based on a particular column and performs calculations such as sum, mean and count.

Q5. What is IQR?

IQR stands for Interquartile Range. It is the difference between the third quartile and first quartile.

Q6. What is an outlier?

An outlier is a value that is significantly different from other values in a dataset.

Q7. What is the use of fillna()?

It is used to replace missing values.

Q8. What is the use of get_dummies()?

It converts categorical data into numerical columns using one-hot encoding.

Q9. What is one-hot encoding?

One-hot encoding converts categories into separate binary columns containing 0 and 1.

Q10. What is the use of drop_first=True?

It removes the first dummy column to avoid redundant information.

Q11. What is the difference between mean and median?

Mean is the average of all values, whereas median is the middle value of sorted data.

Q12. Why do we remove outliers?

We remove outliers to reduce the effect of extreme values on data analysis.

Q13. What is the use of quantile()?

It calculates a specified position or percentile in a dataset.

Q14. What is the use of len()?

It counts the number of records in a dataset.

Q15. Why do we clean column names?

To make column names consistent, simple and easy to access in Python.

